\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Differences along a line of sites}
\date{2026-11-03}


\p{On a line of sites the difference #{\varphi(x+1)-\varphi(x)} is a
linear function of the values of #{\varphi}. Written as a matrix, with
one row for each step and one column for each site, it is the familiar
bidiagonal matrix with #{-1} and #{1} in each row. The second
difference is that matrix multiplied by its transpose. The same array
can be written for any finite carrier once an order of the sites and
of the steps is chosen.}
